.TH MOUSEDEMO 1
.SH NAME
mousedemo \- plot pixels under the mouse
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/mousedemo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I MouseDemo
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/MouseDemo.HC
demonstration, which is eight lines long.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
It plots a single pixel wherever the pointer is, over and over, until
the left button is pressed.
That it plots continuously rather than only on movement is the point:
hold the pointer still and the same pixel is redrawn, sweep it quickly
and the trail is dotted, because nothing is interpolated between
positions.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "left button"
.TP
.B "mouse move"
Move the pen
.TP
.B "left button"
Clear and exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/mousedemo.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR griddemo (1),
.IR wm (1)
